# ===== SAFETY FRAMING =====
th("Quick but important. The flame never touches the resin.")
split("The resin forms a clear holder around a glass candle. The wax burns safely inside the glass.","a clear resin holder with a glass candle sitting safely down inside it","bench","left")
full("a diagram-style shot showing resin on the outside and a glass candle vessel inside","Resin on the outside, real glass candle on the inside. That is the whole safe trick.","close-up")

# ===== TOPIC 1: CHOOSING A SAFE CLEAR CASTING RESIN =====
th("First, the resin. This part matters, so do not skip it.","packing")
full("two bottles of resin, one labelled deep-pour casting resin, one labelled coating resin","You want clear deep-pour casting resin. Not the thin coating kind. Deep pour sets clear and thick.","close-up")
split("Coating resin overheats in a thick block and turns yellow or cracks. Deep pour stays glassy.","a comparison of a yellowed cracked resin block and a perfectly clear one","packing","right")
full("a bottle of resin and a bottle of hardener side by side with measuring cups","Casting resin is two parts. A resin and a hardener you mix in exact amounts. Precision matters.","close-up")
th("Work in a well-ventilated room and wear gloves. Resin is sticky and the fumes are strong.")
full("a tidy workspace with gloves, mixing cups, stir sticks and resin laid out","Set everything out first. Once resin is mixed, the clock is ticking, so you cannot stop halfway.","close-up")

# ===== TOPIC 2: THE MOULD & POSITIONING THE CANDLE =====
th("Next, the mould and getting the candle perfectly placed.","bench")
full("a clear silicone block mould next to a small glass candle","Use a silicone mould a bit bigger than your candle, so resin surrounds it on every side.","close-up")
split("Centre the glass candle. If it sits off to one side, the block looks lopsided.","a glass candle being centred in the middle of a square silicone mould","bench","left")
br("spreads a thin layer of mould release inside a silicone mould with a brush","A little mould release brushed inside means the finished block slides out clean and glassy.")
full("a candle held centred and slightly raised off the bottom of a mould","Raise the candle just off the bottom so resin flows underneath it too. No flat dead spot.","close-up")

# ===== TOPIC 3: MIXING & AVOIDING BUBBLES =====
th("Now the part everyone gets wrong. Bubbles.")
split("Mix the resin slowly and gently. Whipping it fast beats in hundreds of tiny bubbles.","a hand stirring resin slowly with a flat stick in a measuring cup","kitchen","right")
full("a measuring cup of resin with the hardener being poured in to an exact line","Measure exactly by the instructions. Guess the ratio and it stays sticky forever.","close-up")
live("resin being stirred slowly, tiny bubbles rising and a smooth clear liquid forming","the resin swirls slowly and turns from cloudy to clear as it is stirred","Stir slow for a few minutes. It goes from cloudy to crystal clear as the parts combine.")
br("scrapes the sides and bottom of a resin cup with a stick while mixing","Scrape the sides and bottom as you go. Unmixed resin in the corners never hardens.")
full("a heat gun gently passing over the surface of poured resin, bubbles popping","After pouring, a gentle pass with a heat gun brings bubbles up and pops them instantly.","close-up")
split("No heat gun? A hair dryer or even a lighter waved quickly across the top works too.","a hand waving a small flame quickly across the surface of fresh resin","kitchen","left")

# ===== TOPIC 4: POURING IN LAYERS FOR CLARITY =====
th("Here is the secret to a glassy, clear block. Pour in layers.","packing")
full("a deep mould being filled with a first shallow layer of clear resin","Deep pours overheat and cloud if you do it all at once. Thin layers stay perfectly clear.","close-up")
live("a thin layer of clear resin being poured slowly around a centred candle","the clear resin flows in and settles smoothly around the glass candle","Pour a layer, let it firm up, then pour the next. Patience is the whole game here.")
split("Each layer needs a few hours to gel before the next, or they swirl and go cloudy.","two clean clear resin layers setting one on top of the other","packing","right")
full("a mould slowly filling up layer by layer with the candle staying centred","Layer by layer, the candle disappears into a growing block of clear, glassy resin.","close-up")
th("Yes, it takes a day or two. But this patience is exactly why it looks so expensive.")

# ===== TOPIC 5: CURING & DEMOULDING =====
th("Then we wait for the full cure. The hardest part.","window")
full("a filled resin mould curing on a shelf in a dust-free spot","Let it cure fully, usually a day or two. Keep dust off the top while it is still tacky.","close-up")
split("Resin only hardens fully after a complete cure. Pop it early and you dent it forever.","a finger gently testing the firm cured surface of a resin block","window","left")
live("a clear resin block being slowly peeled out of a flexible silicone mould","the silicone peels back to reveal a glassy clear resin block","And then, the best moment. Peeling back the silicone to reveal the finished glassy block.")
full("a freshly demoulded clear resin block with a candle visible inside","Look how clear that is. The candle looks like it is floating inside solid glass.","close-up")

# ===== TOPIC 6: FINISHING =====
th("A quick finish makes it look truly professional.","bench")
br("sands the edges of a resin block smooth with a fine sanding pad","Sand any rough edges smooth. It clouds the surface, but do not worry, we fix that next.")
split("A little polish or a fresh thin top coat brings that sanded surface back to glass clear.","a cloth polishing a resin block back to a glassy shine","bench","right")
full("a perfectly clear, polished resin candle block catching the light","Polished up, the whole block sparkles. It is hard to believe this started as cheap supplies.","close-up")

